  "text": "Frequency Distribution Frequency Distribution For a discrete variable, a frequency distribution consists of the distribution of the number of occurrences for each value of the variable. For a continuous variable, it is the number of occurrences for a variety of ranges of variables. See also: relative frequency distribution , frequency table , frequency polygon .",
